cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lacuna: reproducible brain lesion analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Petersen
    given-names: Marvin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6426-7167"
    affiliation: "University Medical Center Utrecht"
  - family-names: Biessels
    given-names: Geert Jan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6862-2496"
    affiliation: "University Medical Center Utrecht"
repository-code: "https://github.com/m-petersen/lacuna"
url: "https://lacuna-py.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  Lacuna is a scientific Python package and BIDS-App for reproducible analysis
  of brain lesions. It quantifies the impact of focal lesions on brain networks
  and regions — including functional and structural lesion network mapping,
  accelerated functional network mapping, focal damage scoring, and parcel-wise
  aggregation — on standardized MNI reference spaces, fetching the required
  normative connectomes, templates, and atlases on demand.
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-10"
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - lesion analysis
  - lesion network mapping
  - brain mapping
  - BIDS
